# Protein Packed Chickpea Pasta

Based on [https://saucestache.com/the-easiest-protein-packed-pasta-meal-prep-i-make/](https://saucestache.com/the-easiest-protein-packed-pasta-meal-prep-i-make) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251117222514/https://saucestache.com/the-easiest-protein-packed-pasta-meal-prep-i-make/))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Dressing

- [ ] 7 oz (200g) [silken tofu]{ ing="silken-tofu" }
- [ ] 2 tbsp [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }
- [ ] 2 tbsp fresh [parsley]{ ing="parsley" }, chopped
- [ ] 1 tbsp fresh [dill]{ ing="dill" }, chopped
- [ ] 1/4 [red onion]{ ing="red-onion" }
- [ ] 1 clove [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }
- [ ] 1 tbsp [rice vinegar]{ ing="rice-vinegar" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [chia seeds]{ ing="chia-seeds" }

### Pasta and Vegetables

- [ ] 2 [boxes chickpea pasta]{ ing="boxes-chickpea-pasta" }
- [ ] 1 can [chickpeas]{ ing="chickpeas" }
- [ ] 2 stalks [celery]{ ing="celery" }
- [ ] 2 [carrots]{ ing="carrots" }
- [ ] 1/2 cup [peas]{ ing="peas" }

## Recipe

1. Combine [tofu]{ ing="silken-tofu" }, [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }, [parsley]{ ing="parsley" }, [dill]{ ing="dill" }, [red onion]{ ing="red-onion" }, [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, [salt]{ ing="salt" }, [pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }, [rice vinegar]{ ing="rice-vinegar" }, and [chia seeds]{ ing="chia-seeds" } in a bowl. Mix well and refrigerate for at least 5-10 minutes (quick chill while [pasta]{ ing="boxes-chickpea-pasta" } cooks) or 30+ minutes ahead of time to let flavors meld. Remove from fridge and stir before using.
1. Cook [chickpea pasta]{ ing="boxes-chickpea-pasta" } in salted boiling water for 8 minutes.
1. Drain canned [chickpeas]{ ing="chickpeas" } and mash with a fork. Add chopped [celery]{ ing="celery" } and shredded [carrots]{ ing="carrots" } to the bowl.
1. Drain cooked [pasta]{ ing="boxes-chickpea-pasta" } and rinse with cold water.
1. In a hot pan, add [peas]{ ing="peas" }, then [pasta]{ ing="boxes-chickpea-pasta" } on top and mix. Fold in the [chickpea]{ ing="chickpeas" } mixture and chilled dressing. Combine thoroughly and serve.
